// lib_ascent_abr.ks -- the ascent pages' abort-region predictor: the marks on the display and the top-left info
// calculated for this vehicle, not fixed. ATO covers AOA / ATO. The top-left indicator shows GREEN or BLUE instead of
// CONT: GREEN = the contingency steers for an ELS runway, BLUE = none in reach.
// GENERATED offline from the margin tables of the python sims, per boundary (stage 1 flown by kOS's law and the FSSR
// table, not a gravity turn, which keeps no flight-path angle after an SSME out: E TAL ~13 s late; the RTLS line; ATO
// by 4.5.2's retarget), the vehicle dispersed by -3 -2 -1 -0.5 +0 +0.25 +0.5 +0.75 +1 +1.25 +1.5 +2 +3 t on the core
// from SRB sep, one set per SSME variant (the throttle to the SSME out, then the abort level); the E_TAL rows flown
// with the payload FROM LIFTOFF (stage 1 heavy by kOS's law, the delta its stage-1 core formula: flown from SRB sep, a
// heavy payload's E TAL came up to 20 s early at +1 t). delta (m/s) = this vehicle's propellant dV over the nominal's
// at the same VI: stage 2: VISP G0 ln(m / (m - prop)) (prop = the ET over its reserve, asc_tal_check's dV) less the
// set's nominal dV at VI, less the MECO target's change (ASC_VDMAG - ASC_ABR_VD); stage 1: the liftoff mass less the
// reference flight's (MET 1 s) as a change of the core (an ET loaded otherwise than the reference is not told apart
// yet), less the SRBs' dry mass over the I-load's (asc["srb_dd"]: ops1q measures the SRBs on the pad; that mass
// leaves at SRB sep, it is not the core's).
// Frozen at an SSME out (the pages keep the last marks). A boundary's VI = its table at delta (clamped to its
// ends; VI 100000 m/s = never). Computed once a second (asc_abr_tick, the pages).
// The 2EO marks no lower than the droop's VI (lib_ascent_cnt asc_drp_pass's vi_b: a 2EO before it sinks under the
// droop's floor).
// asc_abr_site = THE ONE LOOKUP of the contingency's ELS (the pages' BLUE / GREEN, the 2EO guidance's site).
GLOBAL ASC_ABR_VD IS 3856.2054731546614.   // m/s: the tables' MECO target (ASC_VDMAG when made)
GLOBAL ASC_ABR_MC IS 36.16983.   // t: their core (flight 3: the mass at SRB sep less the ET)
GLOBAL ASC_ABR_M1 IS 515.899865.   // t: flight 3's mass at MET 1 s
GLOBAL ASC_ABR_MD IS 4.796768.   // t/s: its mass flow then
// per SSME variant, picked by the nearest abort level to ASC_KMAX_ABORT once ops1q's asc_ssme_detect has run:
// LIST(abort PL %, nominal PL %, the nominal 3-SSME flight's (VI, dV) m/s pairs, VI rising every 125 m/s, the
// boundaries' (delta, VI) m/s pairs, delta rising)
GLOBAL ASC_ABR_SETS IS LIST(
  // Block II / III: 104 % nominal, 109 % from the SSME out (the dV table linear within 3.67 m/s in stage 2, from 125 s)
  LIST(109, 104, LIST(879.492869, 3612.140926, 1004.492869, 3300.70493, 1129.492869, 3087.434761, 1254.492869, 2902.542404, 1379.492869, 2733.469785, 1504.492869, 2574.722469, 1629.492869, 2423.240539, 1754.492869, 2277.128857, 1879.492869, 2135.107387, 2004.492869, 1996.261237, 2129.492869, 1859.91306, 2254.492869, 1725.547875, 2379.492869, 1592.756181, 2504.492869, 1461.230289, 2629.492869, 1330.710125, 2754.492869, 1200.986291, 2879.492869, 1071.889609, 3004.492869, 943.279631, 3129.492869, 815.02922, 3254.492869, 686.916998, 3379.492869, 558.883218, 3504.492869, 430.874119, 3629.492869, 302.856708, 3754.492869, 174.582632, 3831.690332, 95.284084),
